<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Citicorp Holdings mulls capital increase.</title>
<headline>Argentine Citicorp Holdings mulls capital increase.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's CEI Citicorp Holdings SA said Friday it called an extraordinary shareholders meeting to consider, among other issues, a capital increase of up to $75 million.</p>
<p>The capital increase would be done through the issuing of up to 75 million class B ordinary shares of $1 and one voting right each, CEI told the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>CEI is about 40 percent indirectly owned by Citibank.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
